    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): [ev-763e8d85f263] and the linked PR [ev-870d95b635b4] say Loki 3.0.0 adds sharding for the `avg_over_time` range aggregation. The query is sharded directly when it doesn't group by fewer labels; otherwise it is rewritten as sum-by of sum_over_time divided by sum-by of count_over_time, and those parts are shardable. [ev-a3b2ad6f1bd6] shows the change sits in the LogQL shard mapper (`shardmapper.go`, `range_vector.go`). So applicability can be written as: deployments running LogQL queries that use `avg_over_time` through query sharding, with no new config key or breaking note. Confidence is low because the evidence doesn't say which setting enables query sharding.",
